course: dictionary
lesson: 10316
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word toy can be a thing you play with, a small model of something real, or a verb meaning to play with something carelessly. The context shows you which meaning the writer means.
explain: «Never mix old and new batteries in the same toy.» Here toy is a thing children play with, so it is a noun. «The toy train ran round the track.» Here toy describes a small model of a real train, so it is a describing word that comes before train.
explain: The verb meaning is trickier. «A pet is a responsibility, not a toy.» Think of a pet as a living thing you must look after every day. If you toy with an idea, like «He began to toy with the idea of a new pet», you think about it lightly, without deciding it seriously yet.
fact: Toy can be a noun: a thing children play with, like a doll, a ball or a teddy.
fact: Toy can describe a small model of a real thing, as in «a toy train».
fact: Toy can be a verb: «to toy with something» means to play with it without much care, or to think about an idea not very seriously.
fact: Small toy parts can be dangerous for babies, so always check the age label.
fact: A good check: put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Never mix old and new batteries in the same toy.» What does toy mean here? | *A thing children play with | To play with something carelessly | To think about an idea lightly | A small model of a real thing
exercise: «The toy train ran round the track.» What is toy doing in this sentence? | Meaning to think about a train lightly | Being a thing to play with on its own | *Describing the train as a small model | Being a verb that means to play
exercise: Ella has 12 toys and gives 4 to her cousin. Which action word tells you the sum to do? | toys | *gives | cousin | Ella
test: «He began to toy with the idea of a new pet.» What does toy with mean here? | To buy a whole shop full of toys | To break something by accident | To play with a teddy on the floor | *To think about an idea without taking it very seriously
test: «Keepers sometimes spray perfume or spices in an enclosure, because new smells give cats something to explore, like a new toy.» Why are new smells compared to a new toy? | Cats never like toys | Both are made of perfume and spices | Toys are only for babies | *Both give the cat something exciting to explore
exam: In «a lovely little old round red French wooden toy box», which word gives the opinion? | round | little | wooden | *lovely
